{"path":"atomic/atomic_flag_clear","title":"std::atomic_flag_clear, std::atomic_flag_clear_explicit","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>atomic_flag_clear, <span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>atomic_flag_clear_explicit","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_flag_clear","section":"atomic","kind":"page","summary":"Atomically changes the state of the std::atomic_flag pointed to by obj to clear (false).","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/atomic\">&lt;atomic&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> atomic_flag_clear<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">volatile</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_flag\"><span class=\"kw2109\">std::<span class=\"me2\">atomic_flag</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> obj <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> atomic_flag_clear<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_flag\"><span class=\"kw2109\">std::<span class=\"me2\">atomic_flag</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> obj <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_3\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> atomic_flag_clear_explicit<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">volatile</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_flag\"><span class=\"kw2109\">std::<span class=\"me2\">atomic_flag</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> obj, <br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2113\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order</span></span></a> order <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (3) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_4\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> atomic_flag_clear_explicit<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_flag\"><span class=\"kw2109\">std::<span class=\"me2\">atomic_flag</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> obj, <br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2113\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order</span></span></a> order <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (4) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Atomically changes the state of the <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_flag\">std::atomic_flag</a></span> pointed to by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">obj</span></code> to clear (<code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>).\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1,2)</span> The memory synchronization ordering is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2119\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_seq_cst</span></span></a></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">3,4)</span> The memory synchronization ordering is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">order</span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\"></span> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">order</span></code> is one of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2115\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_consume</span></span></a></span></code>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2116\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_acquire</span></span></a></span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2118\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_acq_rel</span></span></a></span></code>, the behavior is undefined.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> obj\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pointer to <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_flag\">std::atomic_flag</a></span> to access\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> order\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the memory synchronization ordering\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p><code>std::atomic_flag_clear</code> and <code>std::atomic_flag_clear_explicit</code> can be implemented as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">obj<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>clear<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">obj<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>clear<span class=\"br0\">(</span>order<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> respectively.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue2138\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 2138</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++11\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">order</span></code> could be <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"><span class=\"kw2115\">std::<span class=\"me2\">memory_order_consume</span></span></a></span></code>\n</td>\n<td>the behavior is undefined in this case\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_flag\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>atomic_flag</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  the lock-free boolean atomic type <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_flag_test_and_set\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>atomic_flag_test_and_set</span><span>atomic_flag_test_and_set_explicit</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  atomically sets the flag to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code> and returns its previous value <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>memory_order</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  defines memory ordering constraints for the given atomic operation <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(enum)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/atomic/atomic_flag_clear\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>atomic_flag_clear</span>, <span>atomic_flag_clear_explicit</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"atomic","title":"Concurrency support library (since C++11)"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::atomic_flag_clear, std::atomic_flag_clear_explicit","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"4 declarations; revisions: since C++11. Atomically changes the state of the std::atomic_flag pointed to by obj to clear (false)."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"obj, order"},{"label":"Notes","note":"std::atomic_flag_clear and std::atomic_flag_clear_explicit can be implemented as obj->clear() and obj->clear(order) respectively."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"atomic_flag","note":"the lock-free boolean atomic type"},{"label":"atomic_flag_test_and_set, atomic_flag_test_and_set_explicit","note":"atomically sets the flag to true and returns its previous value"},{"label":"memory_order","note":"defines memory ordering constraints for the given atomic operation"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":188,"codeBlockCount":0}
